<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02369</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>01fef4b0-22b6-4774-a366-8df757de2703</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001"><term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">Completing the square</term> can be used to solve quadratic equations.</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><emphasis>Example</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00093">Solve <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">To complete the square to solve an equation, follow these steps:</para>
      <para id="para-00004"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Write the equation in the form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00080"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Complete the square by finding <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00081"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00006"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Add the value to both sides of the equation. </para><para id="para-00082"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00007"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Factor the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">perfect square</term> trinomial and simplify the constants. </para><para id="para-00083"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00008"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Take the square root of each side (remember the plus-minus sign with the constant). </para><para id="para-00084"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math> </para><para id="para-00085"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00009"><emphasis>Step 6</emphasis> - Write two separate equations and solve each. </para><para id="para-00086"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>  or  <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>  or  <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi>–</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00010">Solve each equation by completing the square. In part a, select the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> that will complete the square. In part b, choose the <emphasis>two</emphasis> roots.</para>
      <section id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="_008d3d4f-b998-4f27-83f7-aca8328cfb6b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00011">Enter the value:</para>
            <para id="para-00012"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00013">What is the correct value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> that will complete the square?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00014"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_79029430-6d86-490c-a7d2-3acf7a23fa03" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00016"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00017"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00018">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q#2a-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00019"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00020">What is the correct value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> that will complete the square?</para>
          <para id="para-00021"></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00023">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00024"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->

        <exercise id="_76c1f248-4edb-4a02-9d24-dab54110bcd7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00025"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00026"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00027">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q#3a-->
      
        <exercise id="exer-00002">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00028"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00029">What is the correct value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> that will complete the square?</para>
            <para id="para-00030"></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer: </para>
            <para id="para-00032"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
        </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise id="d20a0059-beb2-4112-8fb1-4ccc23cc7f14" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00033"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00034"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00035">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4bac0056-6a2a-4f4a-ae8f-753e654ff4ae" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          
          <para id="para-00036"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00037">What is the correct value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> that will complete the square?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00038"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="abf2d852-e418-46c5-85cb-845a6773c2b7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00040"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00041"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00042">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e8b33f01-81e0-4dfc-910c-6fc0f6987a44" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          
          <para id="para-00043"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1.6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.63</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00044">What is the correct value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> that will complete the square?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00045"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0.64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="c95204d9-28c9-4d83-a860-91c4b31263a6" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00047"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00048"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00049">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Video: Solve by Completing the Square</title>
        <para id="para-00050">Watch the following video to learn more about solving to complete the square.</para>
        <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
          <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/288db4630304a967aa6e11fd7c31f5115d5f67ad"/>
        </media>
      </section>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
        <para id="para-00051"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_9_3_2_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
       
